{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlJonesMarkovNormalisation","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlNormalisation","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Roots"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.telescope_generalX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.telescope_generalX","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L190-L222","doc":"**Brick 4 / the general-`X` hook telescope.** For the substrate regime\n`Q > 1`, the Macdonald hook telescope holds for **all** `X`:\n\n  `Σ_{|ν|=n} f^ν · schurElement Q X ν.rowLens = ((1 − X)/(1 − Q))^n`.\n\nBoth sides are `eval X` of polynomials in `X` (bricks 2, and the `RHSPoly`); they\nagree at every `X = Q^r`, `r ≥ 1` (brick 3), and `{Q^{r+1} : r}` is infinite\n(brick 1's argument), so `Polynomial.eq_of_infinite_eval_eq` forces the two\npolynomials equal — hence they agree at the arbitrary `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.eval_telescopeRHSPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.eval_telescopeRHSPoly","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L183-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.eval_telescopeLHSPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.eval_telescopeLHSPoly","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L173-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.telescopeRHSPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.telescopeRHSPoly","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L169-L171","doc":"Polynomial-in-`X` lift of the telescope's right-hand side, `((1−X)/(1−Q))^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.telescopeLHSPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.telescopeLHSPoly","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L164-L167","doc":"Polynomial-in-`X` lift of the telescope's left-hand side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.levelBracket_succ_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.levelBracket_succ_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L152-L162","doc":"`[r+1]_Q ≠ 0` for `Q > 0`: the level bracket over a nonempty range is a sum of\npositive powers, hence positive. (Used to invoke brick 3 at `r ≥ 1`, where the\ntelescope agrees; `r = 0` gives `[0]_Q = 0` and is excluded.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.sum_dim_schurElement_rowLens_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.sum_dim_schurElement_rowLens_eq","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L115-L150","doc":"**Brick 3 — the un-normalised agreement at `X = Q^r`.** Summed over the\nSYT-weighted diagrams of size `n`, the List-carrier Schur elements at the\nprincipal specialisation equal `((1 − Q^r)/(1 − Q))^n`. Each term is\n`f_ν · wenzlWeight r Q ν · [r]_Q^n` (carrier bridge + `schurPrincipal = wenzlWeight\n· [r]_Q^{|ν|}`), and `Σ f_ν · wenzlWeight = 1` (the proved general telescope\n`sum_dim_wenzlWeight_eq_one`), leaving `[r]_Q^n = ((1−Q^r)/(1−Q))^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.eval_schurElementPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.eval_schurElementPoly","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L95-L113","doc":"**Brick 2 — the polynomial lift is faithful.** Evaluating `schurElementPoly`\nat `X₀` recovers `schurElement Q X₀ λ`. This makes `schurElement Q · λ` a genuine\npolynomial in its second argument, the premise the identity-theorem route needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.schurElementPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.schurElementPoly","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L88-L93","doc":"Polynomial-in-`X` lift of the whole Schur element: `Q^{n(λ)}` (constant) times\nthe row/cell product of the `cellFactorPoly`s. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.cellFactorPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.cellFactorPoly","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L81-L86","doc":"Polynomial-in-`X` lift of a single cell factor. `cellFactor Q X λ i j` has\n`X` only in the numerator `(1 − X·Q^{c})`; the denominator `(1 − Q^{h})` is\n`X`-free and enters as the constant `C ((1 − Q^{h})⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.powers_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.powers_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MacdonaldTelescopeGeneralX.lean#L61-L75","doc":"**The agreement set is infinite.** For `Q > 1` the powers `Q^n` are strictly\nincreasing, hence distinct, so `{x | ∃ n, Q^n = x}` is infinite — the infinite\nset on which the two telescope polynomials agree, which\n`Polynomial.eq_of_infinite_eval_eq` needs to force them equal. ","signatureChunk":0}]}